   "distinct_observations": 1,
   "has_live_activity": false,
   "pest_types": "",
   "comments": "Upon arrival, I checked in with the store manager, who reported seeing a mouse running around in the back of the store. I immediately performed a thorough inspection of the designated back area, paying close attention to corners, baseboards, and behind equipment. During this inspection, I found no active signs of rodent activity, such as fresh droppings, nesting materials, or rub marks. To prevent any future entry, I identified several potential access points and sealed them completely using steel wool. Specifically, I sealed a small hole in the tile flooring surrounding a white electrical cable penetration. I also packed a gap leading into an open section of a floor drain grate to prevent pests from traveling up through the line. Additionally, I sealed a tight gap found behind a structural junction against the wall paneling, and securely stuffed the open space surrounding a black utility pipe where it penetrates through the textured wall. As a proactive monitoring and trapping measure, I successfully installed two Tin Cat multi-catch mouse traps in strategic locations throughout the back area. I will check these devices during our next scheduled service to monitor for any activity and ensure the perimeter remains secure.",
