   "pest_types": "Fruit Flies",
   "comments": "Upon arrival, I checked in with store manager Juliana, who reported recent sightings of flying insects throughout the retail space. I initiated a comprehensive inspection of the facility, beginning with all rodent monitoring stations. A thorough check of all \"Tin Cat\" live-catch traps revealed zero activity, indicating that current rodent exclusion and baiting measures remain fully effective. Shifting focus to the flying insect issue, my inspection of the trash room revealed a localized population of small flies breeding near the waste receptacles. To address this and prevent further spread, I treated the entire trash room with Alpine WSG, a highly effective residual insecticide. As a proactive preventative measure, I also applied Alpine WSG along all baseboards throughout the back area of the store to create a protective barrier. Given the seasonal pressure and the presence of these flying pests, the current control measures need reinforcement. I highly recommend the immediate installation of at least two additional insect light traps (fly lights) in key transition zones to effectively intercept and monitor fly activity moving forward",
